From: a7a-fedora <241389662+Rabs9@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 12:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pvr_drm: do not dereference a NULL services connection in show_fdinfo

A DRM file on the PowerVR node whose PVRSRV connection is not (or no longer)
established has dfile->driver_priv == NULL. pvr_show_fdinfo() dereferenced it
unconditionally, so reading /proc/<pid>/fdinfo/<fd> of such a file panicked the
kernel ("Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at 0x18",
pvr_show_fdinfo+0x60). systemd-coredump reads the fdinfo of every crashing
process, which turned any userspace crash of a GPU client (a compositor that
failed to initialise EGL, for example) into a hard freeze of the board.

Print only the generic DRM fdinfo keys when there is no connection.
---
 services/server/env/linux/pvr_drm.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/services/server/env/linux/pvr_drm.c
+++ b/services/server/env/linux/pvr_drm.c
@@ -489,6 +489,15 @@ static void pvr_show_fdinfo(struct seq_file *seq_file, struct file *file)
 	my_pid = dfile->pid->numbers[0].nr;
 
 	priv = (struct pvr_drm_private *)dev->dev_private;
+
+	/* No services connection behind this file (opened but never connected,
+	 * or already torn down): nothing driver-specific to report. */
+	if (!pvr_connection || !priv || !priv->dev_node) {
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 5, 0))
+		drm_show_fdinfo(seq_file, file);
+#endif
+		return;
+	}
 
 	/* Generate driver-specific keys */
 	PVRDKFTraverse((DKF_VPRINTF_FUNC*)drm_vprintf,
